Code from other projects in dotLLM's own sources

Parts of dotLLM's own code (its assemblies, and the ptx/ CUDA and spv/ Vulkan kernels shipped beside the executables) are
ported, transcribed or copied from the projects below, under their MIT licences, reproduced here:

* llama.cpp and ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml), including the PrismML fork
  (https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp), which carries the same licence: quantization block layouts, dequantization and
  dot-product kernels, the IQ grid and codebook tables, tokenizer pre-tokenization rules, GGUF metadata handling and other
  routines whose source comments name llama.cpp or ggml.
* tiktoken (https://github.com/openai/tiktoken): the pre-tokenizer regular expressions (cl100k / o200k style) that reached
  dotLLM through llama.cpp's vocabulary code.

